# 116 · A Reviews tab for research runs: every review, each reviewer's answers and comments, and the outcome

**Status:** `IN_PROGRESS` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010) · **Depends on:** [112](112-research-ends-when-answered.goal)

## What

The tabs are built (goal 117's part C2); the owner's approval of them, and a failed try's error kept with its review, are still to come (Progress).

A research run's page and its campaign's page each get a **Reviews** tab. The run's tab lists every review the review panel made of the run's questions, newest first, and opens each one. The campaign's tab lists the reviews of all its runs, by run.

For each review:

- **When and on what:** when it was asked, the evidence it saw (its verified claims, findings and hypotheses at that time), when it was posted, and how many tries it took. Each failed try shows its time and its error, for example `2 of 3 reviewers of the review panel answered (reviewer-2: …)`.
- **Each reviewer:** pass or fail, and its reasons. For each question: whether it found the question answered, its answer with the claims it cites, what it found missing, and each problem code found in the answer (a claim that is not a verified claim of the run, a number that is not in the claims it cites). For each hypothesis: its verdict, why, and the claims it cites. Its field notes, linked to the run's **Journal**.
- **The outcome:** passed, not passed, or the owner's acceptance or rejection with the note. The gaps by question, as the next workers' briefs got them. The owner's messages to the review panel that the review was given, and each reviewer's answer to them.
- **Its cost:** the review's model usage (tokens and time in calls), from what the run's model usage already records.

Between reviews, a question's answer and gaps can be compared, so the owner sees what the run's new evidence changed.

## Why

The owner, 2026-10-24: "be able to review past review panel runs, their comments, and outcomes in a reviews tab for deep research campaigns", for v0.1.1.

On 2026-10-23 a research run's review panel did not pass two reviews and could not post a third. The Overview's **Answer check** line said only that the panel checked a review. The reviewers' comments were in the **Journal** among the workers' notes, and why the third review was not posted was only in the supervisor's log and the run's **Live** view.

## Done when

- [ ] A mockup of the two tabs, approved by the owner.
- [x] The tabs, with tests that each item above shows for a review that passed, one that did not, one with failed tries, and one the owner decided; and that nothing secret shows.
- [x] A failed try's error reaches the harness and is kept with its review (today it is only in the supervisor's log and the run's Live view), so the tab and MCP can show it.
- [x] MCP's `get_run` gives the same details for each review, with its times.
- [x] The pages that describe a run's page, a campaign's page and the review panel.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-24, owner: in v0.1.1, as a tab called Reviews.

## Open questions

- Whether a goal run's reviews of subjective goals (today a short table on its Overview) move into the same tab.

## Progress

- 2026-10-24: Goal written from the owner's words.
- 2026-10-24: Moved into v0.1.0 by the owner, as part of goal 117's redesign of research mode.
- 2026-10-24 09:18 UTC: the tabs are built (branch `feat/117-c2-dashboard`, goal 117's part C2), in the dashboard's existing style. A research run's page has **Reviews** (and **Hypotheses**); its campaign's page has **Overview** and **Reviews**, the latter by run. Each review, newest first, opens to when it was asked and on what (its verified claims, questions and hypotheses: the event that asks it carries no count of findings), when it was posted and by how many reviewers, its tries, its outcome with the owner's decision and note, its cost (the review panel's calls in rounds `review N`: calls, tokens, time in calls and dollars when priced), the decision on each item with its certainty, dissent and the decision before it, each reviewer's verdict, reasons, cited claims and the problems code found, how many field notes the reviewers wrote with it (a link to **Journal**), the owner's messages to the review panel with the answers, and the supervisor's lines for it in **Live**; beside the list, each item's decisions across reviews. Tests: `src/control/research-run-ui.test.ts` (a review not passed, one passed after three tries and accepted by the owner with a note, one waiting with a failed try; an older review; nothing secret; 300 hypotheses and 20 more reviews of five reviewers) and `src/control/research-view.test.ts` (`get_run`). Screenshots from the dashboard demo are for the owner's review: the mockup box stays open until the owner approves them.
- Still to do, outside the dashboard: (1) a failed try's error kept with its review. Today it reaches only the run's **Live** view (the supervisor's unsigned `review N: …` lines, kept while Live keeps the rig's newest 20,000 lines), which the tab shows, but `get_run` cannot. The supervisor would post each failed try to the harness (for example `POST /v1/reviews/<id>/tries` with `{at, error, reviewers_answered}`), and the harness would keep it with the review and send an event such as `review_try_failed` `{review, try, at, error}`, or `review_panel`'s `tries` with `failures: [{at, error}]`; control would then show and give it with no change to its layout. (2) Each reviewer's pass or fail with its reasons as a whole, which only the ledger's review row keeps: `review_items` gives each reviewer's answer per item, and an older review gives only how many reviewers found each question answered. (3) Goal 117's part B2 sends `review_items`, `item_decided` and `review_panel`'s `decided` and `open`; control reads them in the shapes the build design gives.
- 2026-10-24 09:35 UTC: (1) is built. The supervisor posts each try it could not post to `POST /v1/reviews/<id>/tries` (`{try, error}`, the supervisor's token only); the harness checks the review exists and sends `review_try_failed` `{review, try, error}`. Control keeps the newest 20 with the review (`failed_tries`, each with `at`, `try` and `error`): the Reviews tab lists them under **Tries**, `get_run` gives them, and History says each one. An older rig's review still falls back to its lines in **Live**. (3) is done (B2 merged). (2) stays: a reviewer's pass or fail as a whole is in the ledger only. Tests: `src/harness/review-tries.test.ts`, `src/control/research-view.test.ts`, `src/control/research-run-ui.test.ts`.

